To terminate a C program, you can use the return statement to exit the main function. You can also use the exit() function to end the program and return a status code, or call the abort() function to terminate the program abruptly. However, it is generally recommended to use the return statement as it is more graceful and allows you to control the flow of execution in your program.assistant

How do I create a function in C?assistant

Creating a function in C involves specifying the function's return type, name, and parameters (if any) followed by the function body. For example:

// Function declaration 
int sum(int a, int b);

// Function definition 
int sum(int a, int b) {
    return a + b;
}assistant

